 💻 C++ Practice Repository

Hi! 👋  
This repository contains the C++ programs I’ve written while learning and practicing the language.

I created this repo to strengthen my fundamentals, improve my logic-building skills, and keep track of my progress as I explore C++.

---

 📌 What You'll Find Here

This repository includes beginner-friendly C++ programs covering:

- Basic syntax and structure  
- Input and output operations  
- Variables and data types  
- Simple logic-building problems  
- Small mini-projects  

Each program is written with the goal of understanding concepts clearly rather than just completing the task.

---

 📂 Project Structure

```
C-Plus-Plus/
│
├── micro_project.cpp
├── swap.cpp
├── .gitignore
└── .gitattributes
```

### 📄 Program Overview

- **swap.cpp**  
  A simple program to swap two numbers.

- **micro_project.cpp**  
  A small project that applies basic C++ concepts together.

More programs will be added as I continue learning 🚀

---

 🛠️ How to Run the Programs

1️⃣ Clone the repository  
```bash
git clone https://github.com/DiyaPanjwani09/C-Plus-Plus.git
```

2️⃣ Move into the project folder  
```bash
cd C-Plus-Plus
```

3️⃣ Compile any file  
```bash
g++ filename.cpp -o output
```

Example:
```bash
g++ swap.cpp -o swap
```

4️⃣ Run the program  
```bash
./swap
```

